lesystem at /srv/data (backed by /var/lib/srv-data.img, persisted in /etc/fstab with loop,uquota options). Set an XFS user quota of 100MB (soft=hard=100m) for datauser via xfs_quota, so the limit is enforced natively by the filesystem's kernel-level quota subsystem rather than any application logic. Verified enforcement both before and after a full node reboot (writes past 100MB fail with \\\"Disk quota exceeded\\\"; writes under the limit succeed). Completed the mandatory node-restart evidence protocol: captured pre-restart boot_id and quota/data state, issued systemctl reboot, polled until node1 reconnected, confirmed boot_id changed, and confirmed /srv/data auto-remounted with quota intact and data preserved.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Confirmed root fs is XFS with 'noquota' — chose a dedicated loopback XFS filesystem for /srv/data instead of altering root mount options\",\"Installed the quota userspace tools (quota package) on node1\",\"Created datauser account (useradd -m datauser)\",\"Created 512MB image /var/lib/srv-data.img, formatted as XFS\",\"Added persistent fstab entry: /var/lib/srv-data.img /srv/data xfs loop,uquota 0 0 (backed up original fstab to /etc/fstab.bak)\",\"Mounted /srv/data with usrquota active, chowned to datauser\",\"Set XFS user quota: bsoft=100m bhard=100m for datauser via xfs_quota\",\"Verified enforcement: write of 150MB truncated at exactly 100MB with 'Disk quota exceeded'; write of 10MB succeeded\",\"Captured baseline boot_id, mount state, data, and quota report before restart\",\"Issued systemctl reboot on node1 (backgrounded so the ack returned before disconnect)\",\"Polled node1 until exec became available again\",\"Confirmed boot_id changed post-restart\",\"Re-verified /srv/data mount, quota config, and data survived reboot\",\"Re-verified quota enforcement still blocks over-limit writes after reboot, then cleaned up test file\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"datauser account exists on node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d6a9f023e8ae4517\"],\"summary\":\"useradd -m datauser succeeded; id datauser shows uid=1000(datauser)\"},{\"requirement\":\"/srv/data quota is enforced by the filesystem itself (not app-level)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d18f6a98082a49f8\",\"cmd-093e98a56002491b\",\"cmd-de97caeb4a874f91\",\"cmd-01d308cf0f9b4c54\"],\"summary\":\"Built dedicated XFS loopback filesystem, persisted in fstab with uquota option, mounted, and set XFS user quota bsoft=bhard=100M for datauser via xfs_quota\"},{\"requirement\":\"100MB limit enforced for datauser under /srv/data (pre-restart)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1c144a9724e44c59\",\"cmd-6fa3814c5ad04392\"],\"summary\":\"150MB write as datauser truncated at exactly 100MB with 'Disk quota exceeded'; separate 10MB write under the limit succeeded and quota report reflected usage\"},{\"requirement\":\"Healthy baseline captured before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-725f5566f2294415\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 34027437-307c-4f58-bdb2-1fe626bb2d66, confirmed /srv/data mounted with usrquota, data present, and quota report showing 10M/100M\"},{\"requirement\":\"Restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-9010d5f6fbf44945\"],\"summary\":\"systemctl reboot dispatched in background; command returned pid before the node disconnected\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 boot identity changed after restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-445384f4d1c546bc\",\"cmd-36f7fe757f9c473a\",\"cmd-ae31750eb0eb43d6\"],\"summary\":\"Node was unreachable during reboot (connection timeouts), then reconnected with new boot_id 8e10fe6f-7eb2-4f9d-a94d-4f9a64233ef5, differing from the pre-restart boot_id\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery of quota-enforced filesystem and data\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-82cbd592bd1146b1\",\"cmd-604ec241ac1c40b7\"],\"summary\":\"After reboot, /srv/data auto-remounted via fstab with usrquota, prior file (small.bin) intact, quota report unchanged, and over-limit write again failed with 'Disk quota exceeded' confirming enforcement survived the restart\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"On node1, created the datauser account and a dedicated 512MB loopback-mounted XFS filesystem at /srv/data (backed by /var/lib/srv-data.img, persisted in /etc/fstab with loop,uquota options). Set an XFS user quota of 100MB (soft=hard=100m) for datauser via xfs_quota, so the limit is enforced natively by the filesystem's kernel-level quota subsystem rather than any application logic. Verified enforcement both before and after a full node reboot (writes past 100MB fail with \"Disk quota exceeded\"; writes under the limit succeed). Completed the mandatory node-restart evidence protocol: captured pre-restart boot_id and quota/data state, issued systemctl reboot, polled until node1 reconnected, confirmed boot_id changed, and confirmed /srv/data auto-remounted with quota intact and data preserved.","actions_performed":["Confirmed root fs is XFS with 'noquota' — chose a dedicated loopback XFS filesystem for /srv/data instead of altering root mount options","Installed the quota userspace tools (quota package) on node1","Created datauser account (useradd -m datauser)","Created 512MB image /var/lib/srv-data.img, formatted as XFS","Added persistent fstab entry: /var/lib/srv-data.img /srv/data xfs loop,uquota 0 0 (backed up original fstab to /etc/fstab.bak)","Mounted /srv/data with usrquota active, chowned to datauser","Set XFS user quota: bsoft=100m bhard=100m for datauser via xfs_quota","Verified enforcement: write of 150MB truncated at exactly 100MB with 'Disk quota exceeded'; write of 10MB succeeded","Captured baseline boot_id, mount state, data, and quota report before restart","Issued systemctl reboot on node1 (backgrounded so the ack returned before disconnect)","Polled node1 until exec became available again","Confirmed boot_id changed post-restart","Re-verified /srv/data mount, quota config, and data survived reboot","Re-verified quota enforcement still blocks over-limit writes after reboot, then cleaned up test file"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"datauser account exists on node1","command_ids":["cmd-d6a9f023e8ae4517"],"summary":"useradd -m datauser succeeded; id datauser shows uid=1000(datauser)"},{"requirement":"/srv/data quota is enforced by the filesystem itself (not app-level)","command_ids":["cmd-d18f6a98082a49f8","cmd-093e98a56002491b","cmd-de97caeb4a874f91","cmd-01d308cf0f9b4c54"],"summary":"Built dedicated XFS loopback filesystem, persisted in fstab with uquota option, mounted, and set XFS user quota bsoft=bhard=100M for datauser via xfs_quota"},{"requirement":"100MB limit enforced for datauser under /srv/data (pre-restart)","command_ids":["cmd-1c144a9724e44c59","cmd-6fa3814c5ad04392"],"summary":"150MB write as datauser truncated at exactly 100MB with 'Disk quota exceeded'; separate 10MB write under the limit succeeded and quota report reflected usage"},{"requirement":"Healthy baseline captured before restart","command_ids":["cmd-725f5566f2294415"],"summary":"Captured boot_id 34027437-307c-4f58-bdb2-1fe626bb2d66, confirmed /srv/data mounted with usrquota, data present, and quota report showing 10M/100M"},{"requirement":"Restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect","command_ids":["cmd-9010d5f6fbf44945"],"summary":"systemctl reboot dispatched in background; command returned pid before the node disconnected"},{"requirement":"Node1 boot identity changed after restart","command_ids":["cmd-445384f4d1c546bc","cmd-36f7fe757f9c473a","cmd-ae31750eb0eb43d6"],"summary":"Node was unreachable during reboot (connection timeouts), then reconnected with new boot_id 8e10fe6f-7eb2-4f9d-a94d-4f9a64233ef5, differing from the pre-restart boot_id"},{"requirement":"Post-restart recovery of quota-enforced filesystem and data","command_ids":["cmd-82cbd592bd1146b1","cmd-604ec241ac1c40b7"],"summary":"After reboot, /srv/data auto-remounted via fstab with usrquota, prior file (small.bin) intact, quota report unchanged, and over-limit write again failed with 'Di